



Next — Check BIOS recognition of the internal drives
Let's make one read-only check from your current Ubuntu USB terminal.

Run:
sudo lshw -class disk -class storage -short


This shows how Linux identifies the SATA controllers and attached disks.

Then run:
sudo dmesg | grep -Ei 'ata[0-9]|sata|ahci|raid' | tail -30


This checks for storage-controller initialization messages and possible disk errors.

Neither command modifies your drives.
